**What it is** — In 5.3.2, "A Sequential System of Training Means," the authors argue that the development of a specific motor ability "occurs in a specific pattern," so "it is necessary to sequentially improve the functioning of those systems and physiological mechanisms which are crucial for developing a specific motor ability" (PDF p. 302 / printed p. 291). "Progressive functional changes in some systems act as prerequisites for improving the performance of other systems." The rule: "the means used should elicit a definite training effect, but its magnitude should correspond to the body's current level of specific fitness and increase in conjunction with the latter." Hence "the necessity 

### principle--speed-strength-strength-endurance-and-speed-endurance-are-independent-qualities
chapter: "5.1"
